-- title:
--   Disjointness of a chart level set from a w-translate
-- statement:
--   Let $N_0$ be a nonzero natural number, $q$ a prime not dividing $N_0$, and let $\mathfrak P$ be a term of `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`, i.e. a bundled model of the curve `X N₀ q` over $\operatorname{Spec}(R\,q)$ together with its comparison data (properness, flatness, integrality, normality on affine opens, an associated curve model over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with function field `modularFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * q)` and its Galois compatibilities, generic smoothness and geometric integrality, distinguished sections, and in particular the components `𝔓.theta`, a ring equivalence of the chart algebra, and `𝔓.w`, an isomorphism of the model). Write $A =$ `IgusaScheme.chartAlgFin (N₀ * q) q` for the subalgebra of `modularFunctionFieldFull (N₀ * q)` over $\mathbb Z_{(q)}$ consisting of the elements integral over the subalgebra generated by $j$, and $\iota =$ `IgusaScheme.ιFin (N₀ * q) q` for the chart morphism from $\operatorname{Spec} A$ into the model. Let $a, b \in A$ be such that the ideals $(a)$ and $(\mathfrak P.\mathrm{theta}\,b)$ are comaximal, $(a) + (\mathfrak P.\mathrm{theta}\,b) = A$, and let $\mathfrak q, \mathfrak q'$ be primes of $A$ with $a \in \mathfrak q$ and $b \in \mathfrak q'$. Then the point $\iota(\mathfrak q)$ of the underlying space of the model differs from the image of $\iota(\mathfrak q')$ under the map of spaces underlying `𝔓.w.hom`.
--
--   On the finite-$j$ chart of the Deligne–Rapoport model of level $N_0q$ over $\mathbb Z_{(q)}$, the involution $w$ acts through the chart involution `𝔓.theta`; the statement says that the zero locus of $a$ and the $w$-translate of the zero locus of $b$ are disjoint as soon as $a$ and $\theta b$ generate the unit ideal. It is used in the construction of one-sided pools of level polynomials after base change, [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_oneSidedPool_baseChange_of_levelPolynomials`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_oneSidedPool_baseChange_of_levelPolynomials).
